Augmented Leadership & Performance Track Executive Degree Programmes Executive Certificate Programmes Custom Programmes Why Choose EDHEC How to Finance an MBA News Events & Meet-Ups PhD PhD in Finance PhD in Business Management EDHEC Online Research & Faculty Departments Accounting, Control and Law Data Science, Economics & Finance Strategy, Entrepreneurship and Operations Management and Humanities Marketing Faculty Professors and Researchers Research seminars Scientific press review EDHEC Pedagogy Recruitments Centres and Chairs EDHEC Augmented Law Institute EDHEC Climate Institute EDHEC Infrastructure & Private Assets Research Institute EDHEC Quantum Institute EDHEC Artificial Intelligence Centre EDHEC Centre for Responsible Entrepreneurship EDHEC NewGen Talent Centre EDHEC Centre for Net Positive Business Diversity & Inclusion Chair Scientific Climate Indices (an EDHEC Venture) Scientific Climate Ratings (an EDHEC Venture) Leadership Development Chair Family Business Chair Criminal Risks Management Chair Management in Innovative Health Chair Foresight, Innovation and Transformation Chair UNESCO Chair Chair in Geopolitics and Business Strategy Climate Finance Research Publications EDHEC Vox Search Menu Home EDHEC Business School EDHEC Is Recruiting Assistant / Associate Professor of Law Assistant / Associate Professor of law Corps professoral | CDI Lille To apply Back POSITION To participate in the continuous development of the EDHEC programs, EDHEC Business School (www.edhec.edu/en) is recruiting two Assistant or Associate Professors of Law, with research and teaching interests in business law, commercial law, corporate governance, compliance and regulatory issues, international business law, intellectual property law, and related areas. The successful candidate will be expected to develop high-quality, impactful research and contribute actively to teaching across EDHEC’s programs as well as to EDHEC’s pedagogical innovation agenda through active and participatory learning approaches. Location will be on the Lille campus. ABOUT OUR SCHOOL As part of its strategic development, EDHEC is looking ahead to 2050 – a pivotal year for humanity marked by critical challenges such as reducing carbon emissions, protecting biodiversity, addressing inequality, and ensuring universal access to education. By 2050, EDHEC will be graduating students born during the current strategic cycle – young people whose world will depend on the decisions made today. To maximize its societal impact, EDHEC has structured its plan around three strategic priorities: rethinking business models for the common good (I), equipping students to drive transformation (II), and accelerating the development of climate finance (III). The “Generations 2050” plan (2024–2028) is backed by a €270 million investment, including €112 million dedicated to the creation of 90,000 m² of Share & Care campuses. QUALIFICATIONS •    Ph.D. degree •    Evidence of sustained research involvement through case studies and applied academic publications •    Commitment to high-quality teaching and continuous pedagogical development •    Demonstrated ability to teach in academic programs at graduate and undergraduate level •    Energy, dynamism, conviction, open-minded, team-player •    Desire to actively engage in all areas of faculty life •    Personal and professional ethics •    Excellent communication skills •    High level of fluency in English •    Fluency in French and the ability to teach in French are required. At EDHEC, we put diversity at the heart of our practices and know the value of building an inclusive and equitable workplace. Passionate about making an impact on society, we aim to build a team of colleagues representative of the diversity in our communities, and thus strongly encourage all people to apply. Candidates interested in applying for this position are invited to send a cover letter, a resume, a list of publications, a list of classes taught (and evaluations) and the names and contact information of two referees at [email protected] . Inquiries can be addressed to Elie SALAMEH, Head of the Accounting, Control and Law Department, at [email protected] Applications will be considered until the position is filled or February 28, 2026. To apply News 23.09.2026 -  Executive Education EDHEC Global MBA Welcomes Its Class of 2027 to Nice EDHEC Business School has welcomed the Global MBA Class of 2027 to its Nice campus, marking the start of an intensive ten-month journey designed to accelerate professional transformation, broaden international perspectives and prepare participants… Read more 17.09.2026 -  PhD Welcoming the 2026 PhD in Finance cohort to EDHEC A new academic year has begun for the EDHEC PhD in Finance, with the 2026 cohort starting the programme on the Nice campus.This year, 22 experienced finance professionals from 14 different countries have joined the programme, bringing together… Read more 16.09.2026 -  EDHEC EDHEC ranked 14th in Bloomberg’s Best Business Schools in Europe & the Middle East EDHEC Business School’s Global MBA has been ranked 14th overall among European and Middle Eastern business schools in Bloomberg’s latest Best Business Schools ranking. Read more Go to the top of the page MAKE A DONATION About EDHEC EDHEC’s strategy Rankings Research & Faculty EDHEC foundation Entrepreneurship Student Life EDHEC Talents Programmes BBA Master in Management - Grande Ecole ( MiM ) Masters of Science (MSc) MBA & EMBA Executive Education PhD EDHEC Online Our campus Lille Nice Paris London Singapour Others websites Alumni My EDHEC My EDHEC Store Follow-us Facebook Instagram Linkedin YouTube Chat More Contact Pressroom Recruitment Legal notice Privacy Accessibility Home EDHEC Business School Why EDHEC? Key figures History Governance Our Strategy Sustainability at EDHEC Sustainability week 2026 The EDHEC brand Ranking & Accreditations Entrepreneurship EDHEC Entrepreneurs Programmes EDHEC Centre for Responsible Entrepre