xecutive MBA (Part-Time) Healthcare Innovation & Technology Track AI-Augmented Leadership & Performance Track Executive Degree Programmes Executive Certificate Programmes Custom Programmes Why Choose EDHEC How to Finance an MBA News Events & Meet-Ups PhD PhD in Finance PhD in Business Management EDHEC Online Research & Faculty Departments Accounting, Control and Law Data Science, Economics & Finance Strategy, Entrepreneurship and Operations Management and Humanities Marketing Faculty Professors and Researchers Research seminars Scientific press review EDHEC Pedagogy Recruitments Centres and Chairs EDHEC Augmented Law Institute EDHEC Climate Institute EDHEC Infrastructure & Private Assets Research Institute EDHEC Quantum Institute EDHEC Artificial Intelligence Centre EDHEC Centre for Responsible Entrepreneurship EDHEC NewGen Talent Centre EDHEC Centre for Net Positive Business Diversity & Inclusion Chair Scientific Climate Indices (an EDHEC Venture) Scientific Climate Ratings (an EDHEC Venture) Leadership Development Chair Family Business Chair Criminal Risks Management Chair Management in Innovative Health Chair Foresight, Innovation and Transformation Chair UNESCO Chair Chair in Geopolitics and Business Strategy Climate Finance Research Publications EDHEC Vox Search Menu Home EDHEC Business School EDHEC Is Recruiting Associate/Full Professor In Finance, Data Science, Economics, Econometrics, or Related Fields — Nice Campus Associate/Full Professor in Finance, Data Science, Economics, Econometrics, or Related Fields — Nice Campus Corps professoral | Nice To apply Back EDHEC Business School (www.edhec.edu/en) is seeking to recruit one or more senior faculty members and invites applications for the positions of Associate or Full Professor in Finance, Data Science, Economics, Econometrics, or related fields. The position will be located on the Nice Campus. We are interested in accomplished scholars with an established record of research excellence. Fields of specialization may include, but are not limited to, asset pricing, corporate finance, financial econometrics, data science, machine learning, econometrics, quantitative economics, and related areas. Several positions are available across the Nice campus. JOB QUALIFICATIONS: •    Candidates will have completed a Ph.D. in Finance, Economics, Statistics, Data Science, Econometrics, or a closely related field. •    Applicants should have a strong and sustained publication record in top scholarly journals, an active research agenda, and the ability to contribute to the intellectual life of the department. •    The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to teaching at the Bachelor, Master, and Ph.D. levels. •    Fluency in French is not required. ABOUT THE GROUP AT EDHEC Our group is a mix of senior and junior scholars publishing in top academic journals such as American Economic Review, Econometrica, Journal of Econometrics, Journal of Business and Economic Statistics, Journal of Financial Economics, Journal of Finance, Management Science, and Review of Financial Studies. We run several academic seminars and workshops and host a number of leading academics from around the world each year. ABOUT EDHEC EDHEC Business School is one of Europe’s leading business schools and a member of the select group of institutions worldwide to have earned all three international academic accreditations: AACSB, EQUIS, and AMBA. Finance programs at EDHEC are FT ranked in the top 10 worldwide. In order to maximise its societal impact, EDHEC has organised its plan around three main strategic areas: rethinking business models in the service of the common good, the need to educate students to transform, and accelerating the deployment of climate finance. EDHEC values diversity and provides an inclusive and equitable workplace. We offer a competitive salary and benefits package. APPLICATION PROCEDURE: Candidates interested in applying for a position are invited to send a cover letter, a resume, a list of publications, teaching evaluations, and the names and contact information of two referees at [email protected] Inquiries can be addressed to Enrique Schroth, Head of Department of Data Science, Economics and Finance, at [email protected] . Applications will be considered as they are received and until the position is filled or February 28, 2027. To apply News 23.09.2026 -  Executive Education EDHEC Global MBA Welcomes Its Class of 2027 to Nice EDHEC Business School has welcomed the Global MBA Class of 2027 to its Nice campus, marking the start of an intensive ten-month journey designed to accelerate professional transformation, broaden international perspectives and prepare participants… Read more 17.09.2026 -  PhD Welcoming the 2026 PhD in Finance cohort to EDHEC A new academic year has begun for the EDHEC PhD in Finance, with the 2026 cohort starting the programme on the Nice campus.This year, 22 experienced finance professionals from 14 different countries have joined the programme, bringing together… Read more 16.09.2026 -  EDHEC EDHEC ranked 14th in Bloomberg’s Best Business Schools in Europe & the Middle East EDHEC Business School’s Global MBA has been ranked 14th overall among European and Middle Eastern business schools in Bloomberg’s latest Best Business Schools ranking. Read more Go to the top of the page MAKE A DONATION About EDHEC EDHEC’s strategy Rankings Research & Faculty EDHEC foundation Entrepreneurship Student Life EDHEC Talents Programmes BBA Master in Management - Grande Ecole ( MiM ) Masters of Science (MSc) MBA & EMBA Executive Education PhD EDHEC Online Our campus Lille Nice Paris London Singapour Others websites Alumni My EDHEC My EDHEC Store Follow-us Facebook Instagram Linkedin YouTube Chat More Contact Pressroom Recruitment Legal notice Privacy Accessibility Home EDHEC Business School Why EDHEC? Key figures History Governance Our Strategy Sustainability at EDHEC Sustainability week 2026 The EDHEC brand Ranking & Accreditations