ics & Management BSc Admissions & tuition fees Tuition fees & scholarships International Admissions Careers & Studies Meet us Ranking & Accreditations News Master in Management - Grande Ecole ( MiM ) Master in Management - Data Science & AI for Business track Master in Management Business Management Track Master in Management - Finance track Global Master in Management (GETT) News Events Masters of Science (MSc) Finance MSc in Accounting & Finance MSc in Climate Change & Sustainable Finance - EDHEC/MinesParis - PSL MSc in Corporate Finance & Banking MSc in Financial Engineering MSc in International Finance Business & Management MSc in Creative Industries, Entertainment & Arts Management MSc in Data Analytics & Artificial Intelligence MSc in Entrepreneurship & Innovation MSc in Sustainable Business Transformation MSc in Marketing Analytics MSc in Marketing Management MSc in Strategy, Organisation & Consulting LL.M. in Law & Tax Management Marketing MSc in Marketing Management MSc in Marketing Analytics Sustainability MSc in Sustainable Business Transformation MSc in Climate Change & Sustainable Finance - EDHEC/MinesParis - PSL Tech & Data MSc in Data Analytics and Artificial Intelligence MSc in Financial Engineering MSc in Marketing Analytics Innovation & Entrepreneurship MSc in Entrepreneurship & Innovation Law & Management LL.M. in Law & Tax Management Double Degree Programmes MSc in Climate Change & Sustainable Finance - EDHEC/MinesParis - PSL MSc & Global MBA Double Degree News Events MBA & EMBA Global MBA (Full-Time) GMBA Experience in France GMBA & Your Career GMBA Admissions & Fees Executive MBA (Part-Time) Healthcare Innovation & Technology Track AI-Augmented Leadership & Performance Track Online MBA (Part-Time) How to Finance an MBA MBA Insights Alumni Stories Events & Meet-Ups Executive Education Global MBA (Full-Time) GMBA Experience in France GMBA & Your Career GMBA Admissions & Fees Executive MBA (Part-Time) Healthcare Innovation & Technology Track AI-Augmented Leadership & Performance Track Executive Degree Programmes Executive Certificate Programmes Custom Programmes Why Choose EDHEC How to Finance an MBA News Events & Meet-Ups PhD PhD in Finance PhD in Business Management EDHEC Online Research & Faculty Departments Accounting, Control and Law Data Science, Economics & Finance Strategy, Entrepreneurship and Operations Management and Humanities Marketing Faculty Professors and Researchers Research seminars Scientific press review EDHEC Pedagogy Recruitments Centres and Chairs EDHEC Augmented Law Institute EDHEC Climate Institute EDHEC Infrastructure & Private Assets Research Institute EDHEC Quantum Institute EDHEC Artificial Intelligence Centre EDHEC Centre for Responsible Entrepreneurship EDHEC NewGen Talent Centre EDHEC Centre for Net Positive Business Diversity & Inclusion Chair Scientific Climate Indices (an EDHEC Venture) Scientific Climate Ratings (an EDHEC Venture) Leadership Development Chair Family Business Chair Criminal Risks Management Chair Management in Innovative Health Chair Foresight, Innovation and Transformation Chair UNESCO Chair Chair in Geopolitics and Business Strategy Climate Finance Research Publications EDHEC Vox Search Menu Home EDHEC Business School EDHEC Is Recruiting Associate/Full Professor In Strategy Associate/Full Professor in Strategy Corps professoral | CDI Lille To apply Back POSITION To participate in the continuous development of the EDHEC programs, EDHEC Business School (www.edhec.edu/en) is recruiting an Associate or Full Professor of Strategy – Research Track. The senior position requires a good track record in research with publications in top-tier academic journals. The successful candidate is expected to actively teach in EDHEC undergraduate and graduate programs and to fully participate to the EDHEC agenda in Pedagogical Innovations by implementing innovative and active learning approaches. Ability/experience in blended learning and/or e-learning is a plus. EDHEC offers great career development opportunities for Faculty members. EDHEC also offers opportunities for managing programs. Location will be on the Lille campus ABOUT OUR SCHOOL As part of its strategic development, EDHEC is looking ahead to 2050 – a pivotal year for humanity marked by critical challenges such as reducing carbon emissions, protecting biodiversity, addressing inequality, and ensuring universal access to education. By 2050, EDHEC will be graduating students born during the current strategic cycle – young people whose world will depend on the decisions made today. To maximize its societal impact, EDHEC has structured its plan around three strategic priorities: rethinking business models for the common good (I), equipping students to drive transformation (II), and accelerating the development of climate finance (III). The “Generations 2050” plan (2024–2028) is backed by a €270 million investment, including €112 million dedicated to the creation of 90,000 m² of Share & Care campuses. QUALIFICATIONS •    PhD degree •    Evidence of publications in top-tier international journals •    Demonstrated ability to teach in academic programs (undergraduate and graduate) •    Energy, dynamism, conviction •    Desire to actively engage in all areas of Faculty life •    Personal and professional ethics •    High level of fluency in English •    Candidates who possess proficiency in French are encouraged to apply At EDHEC, we put diversity at the heart of our practices and know the value of building an inclusive and equitable workplace. Passionate about making an impact on society, we aim to build a team of colleagues representative of the diversity in our communities, and thus strongly encourage all people to apply. Candidates interested in applying for this position are invited to send a cover letter, a resume, a list of publications, a list of classes taught (and evaluations) and the names and contact information of two referees at [email protected] . Applications will be considered until the positions are filled or February 28, 2027. To apply News 23.09.2026 -  Executive Education EDHEC Global MBA Welcomes Its Class of 2027 to Nice EDHEC Business School has welcomed the Global MBA Class of 2027 to its Nice campus, marking the start of an intensive ten-month journey designed to accelerate professional transformation, broaden international perspectives and prepare participants… Read more 17.09.2026 -  PhD Welcoming the 2026 PhD in Finance cohort to EDHEC A new academic year has begun for the EDHEC PhD in Finance, with the 2026 cohort starting the programme on the Nice campus.This year, 22 experienced finance professionals from 14 different countries have joined the programme, bringing together… Read more 16.09.2026 -  EDHEC EDHEC ranked 14th in Bloomberg’s Best Business Schools in Europe & the Middle East EDHEC Business School’s Global MBA has been ranked 14th overall among European and Middle Eastern business schools in Bloomberg’s latest Best Business Schools ranking. Read more Go to the top of the page MAKE A DONATION About EDHEC EDHEC’s strategy Rankings Research & Faculty EDHEC foundation Entrepreneurship Student Life EDHEC Talents Programmes BBA Master in Management - Grande Ecole ( MiM ) Masters of Science (MSc) MBA & EMBA Executive Education PhD EDHEC Online Our campus Lille Nice Paris London Singapour Others websites Alumni My EDHEC My EDHEC Store Follow-us Facebook Instagram Linkedin YouTube Chat More Contact Pressroom Recruitment Legal notice Privacy Accessibility Home EDHEC Business School Why EDHEC? Key figures History Governance Our Strategy Sustainability at EDHEC Sustainability week 2026 The EDHEC brand Ranking & Accreditations Entrepreneurship EDHEC Entrepreneurs Programmes EDHEC Centre for Responsible Entrepreneurship (ECRE) GENERATIONS powered by EDHEC fund International Strategy Double degrees and international programmes Global Impact Projects International Relations teams International networks International pa