 to fully participate to the EDHEC agenda in Pedagogical Innovations by implementing innovative and active learning approaches. Location will be on the Lille campus. ABOUT OUR SCHOOL As part of its strategic development, EDHEC is looking ahead to 2050 – a pivotal year for humanity marked by critical challenges such as reducing carbon emissions, protecting biodiversity, addressing inequality, and ensuring universal access to education. By 2050, EDHEC will be graduating students born during the current strategic cycle – young people whose world will depend on the decisions made today. To maximize its societal impact, EDHEC has structured its plan around three strategic priorities: rethinking business models for the common good (I), equipping students to drive transformation (II), and accelerating the development of climate finance (III). The “Generations 2050” plan (2024–2028) is backed by a €270 million investment, including €112 million dedicated to the creation of 90,000 m² of Share & Care campuses. QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. degree Evidence of publications in top-tier international journals (kindly add the ABS rank in your CV when providing an overview of your publications – i.e., ABS4*, ABS4, ABS3, ABS2, ABS1) Demonstrated ability to teach in academic programs at graduate and undergraduate level (kindly add teaching evaluations to your application file) High level of fluency in English ánd French, ability to teach in both languages High capacity to develop pedagogical innovation Dynamic, committed, open-minded team-player with a good dose of energy Desire to actively engage in all areas of faculty life Personal and professional ethics Excellent communication skills Visibility in the media is a plus At EDHEC, we put diversity at the heart of our practices and know the value of building an inclusive and equitable workplace. Passionate about making an impact on society, we aim to build a team of colleagues representative of the diversity in our communities, and thus strongly encourage all people to apply. Candidates interested in applying for this position are invited to send a cover letter, a resume, a list of publications (including their ABS rank), a list of classes taught (and evaluations) and the names and contact information of two referees at [email protected] . Inquiries can be addressed to Inge DE CLIPPELEER, Head of the Management and Humanities Department, at [email protected] . Applications will be considered until the positions are filled or February 28, 2027. To apply News 23.09.2026 -  Executive Education EDHEC Global MBA Welcomes Its Class of 2027 to Nice EDHEC Business School has welcomed the Global MBA Class of 2027 to its Nice campus, marking the start of an intensive ten-month journey designed to accelerate professional transformation, broaden international perspectives and prepare participants… Read more 17.09.2026 -  PhD Welcoming the 2026 PhD in Finance cohort to EDHEC A new academic year has begun for the EDHEC PhD in Finance, with the 2026 cohort starting the programme on the Nice campus.This year, 22 experienced finance professionals from 14 different countries have joined the programme, bringing together… Read more 16.09.2026 -  EDHEC EDHEC ranked 14th in Bloomberg’s Best Business Schools in Europe & the Middle East EDHEC Business School’s Global MBA has been ranked 14th overall among European and Middle Eastern business schools in Bloomberg’s latest Best Business Schools ranking. Read more Go to the top of the page MAKE A DONATION About EDHEC EDHEC’s strategy Rankings Research & Faculty EDHEC foundation Entrepreneurship Student Life EDHEC Talents Programmes BBA Master in Management - Grande Ecole ( MiM ) Masters of Science (MSc) MBA & EMBA Executive Education PhD EDHEC Online Our campus Lille Nice Paris London Singapour Others websites Alumni My EDHEC My EDHEC Store Follow-us Facebook Instagram Linkedin YouTube Chat More Contact Pressroom Recruitment Legal notice Privacy Accessibility Home EDHEC Business 