search centres. EDHEC is AACSB, AMBA and EQUIS accredited and regulary ranked among Europe’s top business schools. EDHEC Business School is recruiting an Event, communication & assistant coordinator H/F (permanent contract on Nice Campus). Main tasks You will be primarily responsible for the following missions: Manage and coordinate events: - Prepare all events for the programme (master's in finance track) - Coordinate with the lecturers/adjunct faculty and EDHEC Business School support services - Liaise with the career centre, especially concerning events organised by this department Oversee internal and external communications: - Content creation and liaison between different teams and the academic community during the production of various communication assets (newsletter, interviews and social media posts) - Prepare and follow-up internal and external programme management communications, notably via social media - Implement the graphic identity, in line with EDHEC Business School's graphic charter, and ensure regular updates to the presentation support materials (programme presentations, welcome session presentations...) - Follow-up the programme partnerships with partners and students - Coordinate with the student associations Assist the director with administrative tasks: - Schedule and manage appointments - Handle correspondence and communications - Organize and maintain files and records Profil - Bilingual English/French - Excellent writing skills (in English and French) - Excellent IT and database software skills (expertise in PowerPoint and Excel) - Excellent organizational skills - Flexible (multi-task position in an international environment) - Content management skills - WordPress/Drupal mastery - At least 5 years of proven experience in communication/event/administrative positions To apply News 23.09.2026 -  Executive Education EDHEC Global MBA Welcomes Its Class of 2027 to Nice EDHEC Business School has welcomed the Global MBA Class of 2027 to its Nic