w & Management LL.M. in Law & Tax Management Double Degree Programmes MSc in Climate Change & Sustainable Finance - EDHEC/MinesParis - PSL MSc & Global MBA Double Degree MBA & EMBA Global MBA (Full-Time) Executive MBA (Part-Time) Online MBA (Part-Time) How to Finance an MBA MBA Insights Alumni Stories Events & Meet-Ups Global MBA (Full-Time) GMBA Experience in France GMBA & Your Career GMBA Admissions & Fees Executive MBA (Part-Time) AI-Augmented Leadership & Performance Track Healthcare Innovation & Technology Track Executive Education Global MBA (Full-Time) Executive MBA (Part-Time) Executive Degree Programmes Executive Certificate Programmes Custom Programmes Why Choose EDHEC How to Finance an MBA News Events & Meet-Ups Global MBA (Full-Time) GMBA Experience in France GMBA & Your Career GMBA Admissions & Fees Executive MBA (Part-Time) AI-Augmented Leadership & Performance Track Healthcare Innovation & Technology Track PhD PhD in Finance PhD in Business Management Research & Faculty Departments Faculty Centres and Chairs Climate Finance Research Publications EDHEC Vox Departments Accounting, Control and Law Data Science, Economics & Finance Strategy, Entrepreneurship and Operations Management and Humanities Marketing Faculty Professors and Researchers Research seminars Scientific press review EDHEC Pedagogy Recruitments Centres and Chairs EDHEC Augmented Law Institute EDHEC Climate Institute EDHEC Infrastructure & Private Assets Research Institute EDHEC Quantum Institute EDHEC Artificial Intelligence Centre EDHEC Centre for Responsible Entrepreneurship EDHEC NewGen Talent Centre EDHEC Centre for Net Positive Business Diversity & Inclusion Chair Scientific Climate Indices (an EDHEC Venture) Scientific Climate Ratings (an EDHEC Venture) Leadership Development Chair Family Business Chair Criminal Risks Management Chair Management in Innovative Health Chair Foresight, Innovation and Transformation Chair UNESCO Chair Chair in Geopolitics and Business Strategy undefined Home EDHEC Business School EDHEC Is Recruiting Senior Sales – Climate Risks Data, Analytics & Ratings Senior Sales – Climate Risks Data, Analytics & Ratings Administratif | CDI London To apply Back Senior Sales – Climate Risks Data, Analytics & Ratings Scientific Climate Ratings | An EDHEC Venture Permanent Position – London Position Overview Scientific Climate Ratings is the first climate risk rating agency, born from EDHEC’ renowned academic expertise in finance. Following the landmark sale of Scientific Beta to the Singapore Stock Exchange and the recent acquisition of SIPA by PEI Group, we are now entering an exciting scale up phase. We are hiring a Senior Sales to accelerate the growth of our solutions for financial institutions, corporates and public entities across the UK. You will lead new business development, turning market demand for climate risk intelligence into concrete business outcomes. Reporting to the Head of Sales, you will own the full sales cycle from prospecting to contract, and work together with product, research, and leadership teams. You will also help shape our go-to-market strategy and contribute to thought leadership in a rapidly evolving regulatory and market environment. Key Responsibilities New Business Development Own and drive new business activity across UK and US prospects: financial institutions, asset managers, insurers, corporates, and public sector entities. Identify, qualify, and progress opportunities through proactive market outreach and leveraging your existing UK and US network. You will be responsible for delivering against ambitious revenue targets in the UK and US markets, focusing on high-value, complex sales cycles with senior stakeholders across financial institutions and corporates. Lead discovery sessions, deliver tailored demos and compelling presentations to senior stakeholders. Build and nurture long-term, trusted client relationships that generate recurring revenue and referrals. Continuously refine the go-to-market approach based on market feedback and competitive intellige nce. Commercial Execution Drive pricing proposals and lead contract negotiations through to close. Ensure smooth onboarding and implementation through close coordination with product and technical teams. Collaborate with consulting, product, and modelling teams to tailor solutions and uncover upsell opportunities. Maintain accurate pipeline management in the CRM and deliver regular strategic business reviews to leadership. Market Engagement & Cross-Functional Collaboration Act as the voice of the client internally, translating market insights into product and strategy inputs. Partner with product, consulting, marketing, and leadership teams throughout the sales cycle. Stay current on UK and US regulatory developments, competitive dynamics, and ESG data trends. Represent Scientific Climate Ratings at client meetings, industry conferences, and events to build brand visibility. Support sector-focused campaigns, outreach initiatives, and thought-leadership content. Who You Are You are a commercially driven sales professional with a proven ability to win new business. You combine a client-driven mind with genuine curiosity for climate and finance topics, and you are energised by the idea of selling a product that genuinely matters. You are organised and disciplined in your approach, skilled at managing long sales cycles, and adept at building relationships at senior decision-maker level. You are motivated by client satisfaction and by contributing to the company growth. What You Bring Master’s degree in business, Finance, or a related field Minimum 3+ years of experience in a sales or business development role within financial services, ESG data, or climate finance Strong experience in client-facing roles Proven track record of managing full sales cycles and closing new business Excellent communication, negotiation, and presentation skills Ability to tailor messaging and value propositions to different stakeholders Proactive, fast learner with a strong deal-driven mindset Experience with CRM platforms and account management tools Native English (required), proficiency in an additional European language is a strong plus An existing network within the UK market is a strong advantage What We Offer A senior, high-impact role at the forefront of climate risk intelligence Full ownership of the UK and US sales cycle, with direct access to senior leadership and meaningful input on go-to-market strategy A stimulating environment at the crossroads of rigorous academic research and real-world commercial application Collaboration with world-class researchers, policymakers, and industry leaders Competitive salary and package benchmarked to market standards, reflective of experience Based in our London office at Blackfriars, with a collaborative and international team About Scientific Climate Ratings & EDHEC EDHEC Business School has been recognised for over 20 years for its expertise in finance. Beyond its academic pursuits, EDHEC has ventured into the business world with remarkable success. Notably, it launched \"Scientific Beta,\" a smart index provider sold to the Singapore Stock Exchange for over 200 million euros in January 2020. Following this achievement, EDHEC introduced \"Scientific Portfolio\" and \"Scientific Infra & Private Assets,\" expanding its footprint in analytics and ESMA- regulated financial services.  SIPA has been acquired by PEI Group in March 2026, highlighting again the credibility of such EDHEC ventures for the market. Reflecting its continuous effort to leverage academic and business expertise to make an impact, EDHEC, via its Climate Institute, produces significant research, enabling the creation of new ventures such as Scientific Climate Ratings - the first climate risk rating agency - which brings its unique data and ratings on climate risk financial materiality to the market. Join a fast-growing structure with high ambitions, where proactivity and team spirit are rewarded. As an EDHEC venture, we benefit from EDHEC's academic leadership and propose attractive salaries based on market practices. How to Apply Please send your CV and a brief cover letter (pdf format) explaining your interest in the role and how your background aligns with our mission. To apply News 23.09.2026 -  Executive Education EDHEC Global MBA Welcomes Its Class of 2027 to Nice EDHEC Business School has welcomed the Global MBA Class of 2027 to its Nice campus, marking the start of an intensive ten-month journey designed to accelerate professional transformation, broaden international perspectives and prepare participants… Read more Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Teams WeChat 17.09.2026 -  PhD Welcoming the 2026 PhD in Finance cohort to EDHEC A new academic year has begun for the EDHEC PhD in Finance, with the 2026 cohort starting the programme on the Nice campus.This year, 22 experienced finance professionals from 14 different countries have joined the programme, bringing together… Read more Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Teams WeChat 16.09.2026 -  EDHEC EDHEC ranked 14th in Bloomberg’s Best Business Schools in Europe & the Middle East EDHEC Business School’s Global MBA has been ranked 14th overall among European and Middle Eastern business schools in Bloomberg’s latest Best Business Schools ranking. Read more Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Teams WeChat Go to the top of the page MAKE A DONATION About EDHEC EDHEC’s strategy Rankings Research & Faculty EDHEC foundation Entrepreneurship Student Life EDHEC Talents Programmes BBA Master in Management - Grande Ecole ( MiM ) Masters of Science (MSc) MBA & EMBA Executive Education PhD EDHEC Online Our campus Lille Nice Paris London Singapour Others websites Alumni My EDHEC My EDHEC Store Follow-us Facebook Instagram Linkedin YouTube Chat More Contact Pressroom Recruitment Legal notice Privacy Accessibility Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More…"
